From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Drag and drop into Wine windows.

Files dragged from the desktop (Dolphin, Nautilus) could not be dropped into Wine windows under
Wayland: the wl_data_device enter, motion, drop and leave events were ignored, and with a
compositor that offers zwlr_data_control (KWin) there was no wl_data_device at all.

A wl_data_device for drag and drop is made also when the clipboard uses data control. When a
drag enters a window its data is read, text/uri-list as CF_HDROP and UTF-8 text as
CF_UNICODETEXT (a stuck source gives up after 2 s, as this thread reads all Wayland events),
and the thread of the window passes the drag on to user32 like winex11 does for XDnD: enter,
drag at each motion, drop, leave. The answer of the drop target accepts or refuses the drag
for the source; user32's patch 0002 gives late targets such as Unreal Engine a grace period.

